{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites","id":168761,"title":"Idigam Chronicle Weekly Discussion: Rites","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-14T03:59:05-07:00","id":168761,"title":"Idigam Chronicle Weekly Discussion: Rites","content":"And now we return to our <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ritualistic/\" target=\"_blank\">weekly scheduled open development</a>, after a brief delay in the democratic process.<br /> <br /> I for one am deeply pleased with the new personalized direction rites are taking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T04:41:02-07:00","id":168786,"title":"","content":"I have only one major complaint.<br /> <br /> That this isn't how the Ceremony system for Geist worked <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T06:32:23-07:00","id":168850,"title":"","content":"This strengthens my belief that the Bound and the Forsaken are close cousins XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T07:04:43-07:00","id":168871,"title":"","content":"Well, all those rites seem quite remarkable, I guess there won't be any more of this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Come on, you're our ritualist, you MUST have something useful for us!&quot;<br /> &quot;Sure. Care to help me prepare the Funeral rite?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T07:14:03-07:00","id":168897,"title":"","content":"There are 23 rites in the draft I submitted, including at least 4 at each dot rank (so there's plenty of choice amongst both low-dot and high-dot rituals). Obviously this is first draft, may change, etc, especially since I went over word count a bit, but I specifically tried to make every rite something that has mechanical impact and cut out all the 'arcane paperwork' rites. Of the rites that survived the chopping block, there was quite a bit of merging of extremely similar concepts; so, as you can see, there's no more Banish Human and Banish Spirit, just Banish; the new Sacred Hunt is a merging of the old Sacred Hunt and the Blessing of the Spirit Hunt, etc. There's quite a few new capabilities in the Rites list as well now.<br /> <br /> One of my main aims is to make players look at the rites list and feel they want to play a ritemaster because it's cool and powerful and interesting, not that the pack needs a ritemaster just to deal with ritual bureaucracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T07:18:48-07:00","id":168900,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I'm interested in feedback on the rites that have been revealed as well. Particularly about their desirability - can you see your characters taking them and using them? Totemic Empowerment is one that I'm having a hard time figuring out if I've gotten right, in terms of what it gives you as opposed to what it takes away (namely your totem's independence for the duration of the rite).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T07:41:31-07:00","id":168922,"title":"","content":"Personally, I find Banish is a little too long for me. Banishing a dangerous spirit/human/whatever as 1 roll per minute is a little slow, for an urgency like that. I think a &quot;turn per roll&quot; would much more valuable.<br /> <br /> Totemic empowerment is remarkable and memorable (meaning you won't forget having it anytime soon), and I think that is enough.<br /> <br /> One thing I noticed: some gifts, like Sly hunter (Half moon 3), only work in <i>Siskur-Dah</i>. That means that if you don't have the <i>Siskur-dah</i> rite, the Gift is plain useless. I don't know if any of you changed this, but I think it's not a good design to make gifts work only when <i>Siskur-dah</i> has been cast. Those gifts should probably have at least some kind of effect even without <i>Siskur-dah</i><i>.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T07:46:24-07:00","id":168924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=168900#post168900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and I'm interested in feedback on the rites that have been revealed as well. Particularly about their desirability - can you see your characters taking them and using them? Totemic Empowerment is one that I'm having a hard time figuring out if I've gotten right, in terms of what it gives you as opposed to what it takes away (namely your totem's independence for the duration of the rite).</div> </div> </div> </div> That would be difficult to judge, not knowing what benefits a pack gains from an independent totem <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T07:48:08-07:00","id":168925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=168922#post168922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I find Banish is a little too long for me. Banishing a dangerous spirit/human/whatever as 1 roll per minute is a little slow, for an urgency like that. I think a &amp;quot;turn per roll&amp;quot; would much more valuable. Totemic empowerment is remarkable and memorable (meaning you won't forget having it anytime soon), and I think that is enough. One thing I noticed: some gifts, like Sly hunter (Half moon 3), only work in <i>Siskur-Dah</i>. That means that if you don't have the <i>Siskur-dah</i> rite, the Gift is plain useless. I don't know if any of you changed this, but I think it's not a good design to make gifts work only when <i>Siskur-dah</i> has been cast. Those gifts should probably have at least some kind of effect even without <i>Siskur-dah</i><i>.</i></div> </div> </div> </div> I'm pretty sure Siskur-Dah the sacred hunt, and Sacred Hunt the rite are different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T07:49:55-07:00","id":168926,"title":"","content":"I think Totemic Empowerment is ok, especially as it is a one-dot rite. When in the shadow, the trade-off probably would not be worth it. But if your totem isn't adept at fighting in the material, then using the Totem to strengthen one of the pack-members seems like a good choice there. It also allows for some nice suprise tactics, if the totem is bound into one of your mortal or wolfblooded packmates that the enemy does not know about (and it could also give wolfblooded players more options, temporarily).<br /> <br /> EDIT: When thinking some more about it, maybe the attribute bonusses should be a little higher, to offset the loss of the totem as an extra character. One option is using something like the old claiming rules, where the spirit's Power was distributed over the character's Power Attributes, and so on. This has the extra benefit of the character to use these rites for less physical tasks. But the problem then is that the power has too few downside, and is too powerful for a one-dot rite...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":". 06-14-2014, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T07:50:40-07:00","id":168928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=168925#post168925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm pretty sure Siskur-Dah the sacred hunt, and Sacred Hunt the rite are different things.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Sacred Hunt (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> The sacred hunt, the <i>Siskur-Dah</i>, is the most holy of all rites. It is said to be founded upon the laws of the hunt that the Wolf-Mother herself personified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T08:29:00-07:00","id":168948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=168928#post168928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Sacred Hunt (\u2022\u2022)</b> The sacred hunt, the <i>Siskur-Dah</i>, is the most holy of all rites. It is said to be founded upon the laws of the hunt that the Wolf-Mother herself personified.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, I read that, but I don't think it's meant to imply that this rite is the only way to perform the Sisku-Dah. Like how all squares are rectangles but not all rectangles are squares, you can perform the Siskur-Dah without this rite, but the rite can only apply to the Siskur-Dah. At least, that's what I imagine the intent was, because it would be bizarre if some Gift Facets couldn't be used unless a member of your pack has a specific two-dot ritual. Technically the wording doesn't support my interpretation, but it is a first draft. I highly doubt the intention was for this to be the only way to perform the Siskur-Dah","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T08:47:37-07:00","id":168956,"title":"","content":"Well, personally I'd have preferred the Siskur-dah to be simply something a pack can do, like &quot;shapeshifting&quot; or &quot;having a totem&quot;, what in FWC would be called an &quot;attainment&quot;, not a full blown rite. An integral part of being a werewolf. But hey, I would be fine if the Gifts that involve Siskur-Dah didn't need the rite to work, but worked better anyway with the rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T08:51:39-07:00","id":168961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=168956#post168956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, personally I'd have preferred the Siskur-dah to be simply something a pack can do, like &amp;quot;shapeshifting&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;having a totem&amp;quot;, what in FWC would be called an &amp;quot;attainment&amp;quot;, not a full blown rite. An integral part of being a werewolf. But hey, I would be fine if the Gifts that involve Siskur-Dah didn't need the rite to work, but worked better anyway with the rite.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's kind of what I mean, I figure the Siskur-Dah is just a thing that werewolves do, they go out and ritualistically hunt their prey, and any such act will, in my games, be considered Siskur-Dah for the purposes of Gifts and such. Sacred Hunt is just a rite you can perform to enhance the Siskur-Dah, just like certain Gifts enhance it. I imagine that was the intention, as I can't picture such a central aspect of the new wolf-must-hunt direction being relegated to a single specific two-dot Gift in order to perform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T09:03:38-07:00","id":168972,"title":"","content":"As of the rules I've used, I've innately allowed Werewolves to get Essence back (equal to the prey's Rank) for a successful Hunt. I'd be cool with having that in the rules, but if you did a, say, <i>Bounty of the Sacred Hunt</i> Rite, it allowed you to also devour the Spirit's remaining Essence and split it between the pack, and the other things mentioned; that'd be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T10:15:01-07:00","id":168997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=168961#post168961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's kind of what I mean, I figure the Siskur-Dah is just a thing that werewolves do, they go out and ritualistically hunt their prey, and any such act will, in my games, be considered Siskur-Dah for the purposes of Gifts and such. Sacred Hunt is just a rite you can perform to enhance the Siskur-Dah, just like certain Gifts enhance it. I imagine that was the intention, as I can't picture such a central aspect of the new wolf-must-hunt direction being relegated to a single specific two-dot Gift in order to perform.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my interpretation as well, though it'd be nice to get confirmation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T10:48:16-07:00","id":169026,"title":"","content":"I gotta agree on the Banish thing. I could see a spirit standing still for a few minutes if you had a ban for it, but most things would just run away. Perhaps a sidebar explaining that the rite has tagged on so it doesn't matter if they run? Or otherwise?<br /> <br /> Also, I don't like the Wound spirits going somewhere else. Wound spirits should be spirits like the others. Unless Wounds have changed, it seems less like spirits are the reflections of everything in the real world, and more like spirits are the reflections of everything in the real world, except bad spirits which come from some other place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-14-2014, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T11:11:05-07:00","id":169033,"title":"","content":"I liked this update. Making rites unique and better yet using a variety of customization dice pools makes it feel like rites are useful for every one not just Itheaurs.<br /> <br /> The one thing I didn't like is the Chain Rage rite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164708#post164708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rite of Dedication was an example of an 'admin' rite, and one that existed purely to patch a hole. It did so via adding an additional bit of bean-counting to the system (how many Dedicated items can I have/do I currently have?), was essentially a mandatory rite that your Ithaeur had to take or else everyone was constantly running to the charity shops to buy some cheap new clothes, and didn't really add anything to the game.<br /> <br /> The area of the game that Dedication used to cover has been folded into another element of the IC mechanics and is both a) far simpler and b) doesn't require an admin rite that someone has to take.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what the Chain Rage rite feels like. It's purpose is patch a hole. It adds additonal bit of bean-counting to the system (how many days left until my chain is not longer useful?), it's a mandatory rite that your ritemaster has to take otherwise every one is constantly kuruthing every night and doesn't really add anything to the game.<br /> <br /> Edit: Rather than making a rite to fix the Kuruth system, just fix the Kuruth system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3300-a-bigger-thicker-dick","name":"A Bigger Thicker Dick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T11:13:05-07:00","id":169035,"title":"","content":"Re: Totemic Empowerment, I don't think it makes sense to have the 'buff' dots to strength, etc. be consistent across all totemkind, since your totem of the library will have different strengths than your wild bull. Also, re: the last bullet of that rite, its losing control during the rite that dings your harmony, not the rite itself? I had to read it twice to make sure. Re: rites in general, I love the flexibility! The idea of multiple packs having a different rite and opinion of the rite... The guys who use brawl+stamina to endure pain vs the ones that bravado themselves into invulnerability with strength+expression or the like... Good stuff :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T11:37:43-07:00","id":169048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169026#post169026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I don't like the Wound spirits going somewhere else. Wound spirits should be spirits like the others. Unless Wounds have changed, it seems less like spirits are the reflections of everything in the real world, and more like spirits are the reflections of everything in the real world, except bad spirits which come from some other place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wound Spirits should, per Inferno, go back to the, well, Inferno. It was established that they are corrupted Spirits and are now of the Inferno, that is to say Demons, now instead of spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T11:39:41-07:00","id":169050,"title":"","content":"Nah chain the rage works. Remember the forsaken are supposed to be big scary rage monsters. With that in mind, chain the rage helps them from going completely ape-shit every two seconds. Then they can safely blood rage elsewhere. It works for what it is and I rather enjoy it.<br /> <br /> That said I'm greatly curious to see how rite of dedication changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T11:47:51-07:00","id":169060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169050#post169050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said I'm greatly curious to see how rite of dedication changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I can help you with that curtsey of a developer post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/163370-ritemasters?p=164708#post164708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rite of Dedication was an example of an 'admin' rite, and one that existed purely to patch a hole. It did so via adding an additional bit of bean-counting to the system (how many Dedicated items can I have/do I currently have?), was essentially a mandatory rite that your Ithaeur had to take or else everyone was constantly running to the charity shops to buy some cheap new clothes, and didn't really add anything to the game.<br /> <br /> The area of the game that Dedication used to cover has been folded into another element of the IC mechanics and is both a) far simpler and b) doesn't require an admin rite that someone has to take.</div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T11:49:53-07:00","id":169061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169048#post169048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wound Spirits should, per Inferno, go back to the, well, Inferno. It was established that they are corrupted Spirits and are now of the Inferno, that is to say Demons, now instead of spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except every Wound spirit being an immundi (the half demon, half spirit demons from Inferno) implies that 'bad' spirits don't belong in the spirit. Because, what? Evil can't exist without demons causing it? Is the World of Darkness all happy and cheerful except for where those bad guys that live somewhere else? Inferno also mentions that it's impossible to tell the difference between an immundi and a regular spirit (or any of the diaboli and their 'normal' versions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-14-2014, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T12:11:12-07:00","id":169103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169050#post169050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah chain the rage works. Remember the forsaken are supposed to be big scary rage monsters. With that in mind, chain the rage helps them from going completely ape-shit every two seconds. Then they can safely blood rage elsewhere. It works for what it is and I rather enjoy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason it needs to be a separate, mandatory, bean-counting rite though. Place the effects of the rite into the Kuruth system and it streamlines things much more. Every werewolf in soft rage can leave it if they score 5 successes on their extended Resolve + Composure to increase time limit. It keeps the theme of them raging and struggling to control that rage with out unnecessary complications.<br /> <br /> It should be removed for the same reason Rite of Dedication was removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3301-the-inevitable","name":"The Inevitable","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T12:12:01-07:00","id":169104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=168897#post168897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are 23 rites in the draft I submitted, including at least 4 at each dot rank (so there's plenty of choice amongst both low-dot and high-dot rituals). Obviously this is first draft, may change, etc, especially since I went over word count a bit, but I specifically tried to make every rite something that has mechanical impact and cut out all the 'arcane paperwork' rites. Of the rites that survived the chopping block, there was quite a bit of merging of extremely similar concepts; so, as you can see, there's no more Banish Human and Banish Spirit, just Banish; the new Sacred Hunt is a merging of the old Sacred Hunt and the Blessing of the Spirit Hunt, etc. There's quite a few new capabilities in the Rites list as well now.<br /> <br /> One of my main aims is to make players look at the rites list and feel they want to play a ritemaster because it's cool and powerful and interesting, not that the pack needs a ritemaster just to deal with ritual bureaucracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wanna shorten the word count a bit? take off some symbols. I'm looking at way too many symbols in the preview already. It make customization fucking complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T12:13:40-07:00","id":169106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169061#post169061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except every Wound spirit being an immundi (the half demon, half spirit demons from Inferno) implies that 'bad' spirits don't belong in the spirit. Because, what? Evil can't exist without demons causing it? Is the World of Darkness all happy and cheerful except for where those bad guys that live somewhere else? Inferno also mentions that it's impossible to tell the difference between an immundi and a regular spirit (or any of the diaboli and their 'normal' versions).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, impossible to tell <i>physically. </i>Demons think like humans, and that's not <i>too </i>difficult to suss out (or their unique Numina).<br /> <br /> Also, nice strawman. The Inferno is a type of evil that explicitly does <i>not </i>belong in the world, it's part of the same dark cosmos the Strix are likely from - not something that <i>shouldn't </i>exist, but definitely something that poses a danger to everyone not part of it. Also, they <i>feed</i> on Vice and nasty, related things, and apart from a little &quot;gardening&quot;, they're symptoms of a problem, not the core problem - though symptoms are the thing that kills you. So it was before Inferno, so it is after - Lore of the Forsaken explicitly described Maeljin as living in their own pocket of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Wounds are described as &quot;infections&quot; for a reason, and infections require sterilization. It's a symptom of the worst imbalance there is, minus truly alien things like idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T12:26:14-07:00","id":169117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169106#post169106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, impossible to tell <i>physically. </i>Demons think like humans, and that's not <i>too </i>difficult to suss out (or their unique Numina).</div> </div> </div> </div>'Unfortunately, it\u2019s also impossible to use a supernatural power to tell a Diabolus apart from an ordinary ghost or spirit. Its worldly essence camouflages it from these abilities.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wounds are described as &quot;infections&quot; for a reason, and infections require sterilization. It's a symptom of the worst imbalance there is, minus truly alien things like idigam. </div> </div> </div>Well, ignoring the fact that now you can just banish the spirits from it, once again this is implying that evil doesn't come from our world, it comes from another place, which according to you is part of a 'dark cosmos,' instead of being reflections of the 'real' World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T12:27:13-07:00","id":169119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169061#post169061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except every Wound spirit being an immundi (the half demon, half spirit demons from Inferno) implies that 'bad' spirits don't belong in the spirit. Because, what? Evil can't exist without demons causing it? Is the World of Darkness all happy and cheerful except for where those bad guys that live somewhere else? Inferno also mentions that it's impossible to tell the difference between an immundi and a regular spirit (or any of the diaboli and their 'normal' versions).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even by core not all 'bad' spirits are Wound spirits. A murder-spirit is a natural, albeit scary, spirit; not a Wound spirit. Wounds are... not natural. That's why they are scary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf: the Forsaken core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where the spirit world has been even more grievously damaged by atrocity, it bleeds out resonance of particularly negative aspect and gives birth to spirits of the worst sort. These places are called Wounds, where the spirit wilds are not simply injured, but infected. ... A Wound might form anywhere that cruelty, suffering or hatred are at their worst \u2014 a vivisection lab, a concentration camp, a prison overseen by a particularly cruel and hateful staff, a brutal mental hospital. The cruel spirits of negative concepts such as pain, hatred, suffering and despair are the maggots that write within these infected gashes in the Shadow. But as malevolent as these spirits that thrive on suffering may seem, the grim truth is that they are not the cause of the misery that feeds them \u2014 merely the symptom.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the Core, Wounds are places where things are so bad in the Flesh that they cause an infection of negativity. Not a lot there. Now, to Inferno...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inferno</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To werewolves, demons are spirits that have fallen so far from the natural order they should not exist, but even in a parody of true life, they\u2019ve proven to be as adaptable and mutable as real, living things. They are too corrupt to survive in this world for long, so they create corruption, and breathe it like a nurturing atmosphere. They create Wounds in the world, and grow so foul even the First Tongue, the song of nature itself, fails to define them, and they teach their servants an ugly name: Maeljin.<br /> ...<br /> <br /> Werewolves know evil things spill forth from Wounds in the Shadow. These sorts of creatures are most likely to be Diaboli. They are lords of hate, vengeful ghosts, Shadow reflections of places that have been wounded by atrocities.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, there you go.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 06-14-2014, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T12:34:43-07:00","id":169122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=168922#post168922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I find Banish is a little too long for me. Banishing a dangerous spirit/human/whatever as 1 roll per minute is a little slow, for an urgency like that. I think a &quot;turn per roll&quot; would much more valuable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been musing over this one. I <i>think </i>1 roll per minute should be fine, since the target will likely be hit in one or two rolls; this means you need to keep the target in... ah, I don't think I gave a solid definition on range and targeting, did I? Anyway, presume that you don't need the target to stay dead still, just need to keep them in perception range. It means that Banishment isn't an instant-success button for bumping beings back into their realm, and you need to take some effort to keep them in place; get the rest of the pack to keep a Shadow-intruder in place, or use the Bane material of a spirit to hem it in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One thing I noticed: some gifts, like Sly hunter (Half moon 3), only work in <i>Siskur-Dah</i>. That means that if you don't have the <i>Siskur-dah</i> rite, the Gift is plain useless. I don't know if any of you changed this, but I think it's not a good design to make gifts work only when <i>Siskur-dah</i> has been cast. Those gifts should probably have at least some kind of effect even without <i>Siskur-dah</i><i>.</i> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Siskur-Dah Gifts etc will require the Rite. This is first draft stuff and Stew is working hard in the redlining to get everything straight and connect all the dots. I just grabbed hold of the Siskur-Dah thematics hard for the rite since it seemed most appropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=168924#post168924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That would be difficult to judge, not knowing what benefits a pack gains from an independent totem <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much the same as what you have now - the benefit of an additional pack member with some unusual powers and the ability to be in Twilight etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T12:54:13-07:00","id":169148,"title":"","content":"Derp. I wrote a long reply to various people then accidentally deleted it. Let's try again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169026#post169026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I don't like the Wound spirits going somewhere else. Wound spirits should be spirits like the others. Unless Wounds have changed, it seems less like spirits are the reflections of everything in the real world, and more like spirits are the reflections of everything in the real world, except bad spirits which come from some other place.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Wounded spirits aren't 'bad' spirits. They're <i>corrupted</i>. Hatred, anger, death, murder, pain, anguish spirits are all perfectly normal spirits. The creatures that infest the pustules of taint that are Wounds have been infected and changed. A Wounded spirit of happiness would be hurled through a Wound by the Banish rite; an unWounded spirit of hatred would not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Bigger Thicker Dick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169033#post169033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly what the Chain Rage rite feels like. It's purpose is patch a hole. It adds additonal bit of bean-counting to the system (how many days left until my chain is not longer useful?), it's a mandatory rite that your ritemaster has to take otherwise every one is constantly kuruthing every night and doesn't really add anything to the game.<br /> <br /> Edit: Rather than making a rite to fix the Kuruth system, just fix the Kuruth system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I can happily assure you that the purpose I had in mind for Chain Rage was not to patch any holes. Uratha will not be constantly Kuruthing every night and I'm not really sure why you'd think they would be.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the purpose of Chain Rage is to offer a trade-off option. On the one hand, it offers a solid second line of protection should Kuruth occur, giving werewolves a solid chance of avoiding entering full Death Rage. However, it does this in return for two things. The first is the certainty of full-on Death Rage at the end of the month. <i>This</i> is supposed to be something that, of course, packs who use Chain Rage will plan around and keep an eye on; you probably want to have some sort of secure place to lock the chap into when it comes to the end of their month under the rite, then let them loose somewhere they can't destroy anything. This, er, may be problematic if they have certain Facets, of course. The second trade-off, though, is the fact you have to have the focus on you. This is a vulnerability - if that focus gets taken or destroyed, boom, death rage. Again, I'd expect packs to do everything they can to protect their rage foci as much as possible, but that doesn't mean the risk isn't there. Canny enemies and pure bad luck can both cause a serious back-fire here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169050#post169050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said I'm greatly curious to see how rite of dedication changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's gone, dead. Mechanics for stuff shifting with you are now part of the core shapeshifting rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169060#post169060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe I can help you with that curtsey of a developer post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a writer, not a dev! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169104#post169104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wanna shorten the word count a bit? take off some symbols. I'm looking at way too many symbols in the preview already. It make customization fucking complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly the reduced wordcount would be tiny :P<br /> <br /> I'm currently eyeing the symbol lists and we're playtesting the rites in my Monday game. I'm probably going to aim for 4-5 symbols per rite in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T13:07:40-07:00","id":169169,"title":"","content":"I am rather astounded at how much people think Mass Kuruth is actually an issue. I don't even have any particularly unique insight on the project and I can tell it's going to be fairly manageable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T13:11:48-07:00","id":169171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much the same as what you have now - the benefit of an additional pack member with some unusual powers and the ability to be in Twilight etc.</div> </div> </div> </div> I figured, I was just pulling your leg. Totems and the mechanics of totem creation have been on my mind since I'm doing some preliminary NPC pack building for the game I'm going to run once IC is out, and I couldn't resist. Anyway, I like the idea behind the rite. I think it could stand to be pushed a little more, just because you're giving up a pack mate (and one that uses the ephemeral entity stats, no less) to get the bonuses. But conceptually it's awesome, and I'd say in its current form it's tempting in the right situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T13:18:18-07:00","id":169176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169117#post169117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Unfortunately, it\u2019s also impossible to use a supernatural power to tell a Diabolus apart from an ordinary ghost or spirit. Its worldly essence camouflages it from these abilities.'<br /> <br /> <b>Who says I was talking about <u>supernatural</u> powers? Psychological manipulation and pressing it works wonders. That, and the text doesn't realize a demon can't control its Lord of Lies ability - if supernatural senses are fooled by something you already know is untrue, it doesn't take long to realize the creature that told you is a native of the Hot Place.</b><br /> <br /> Well, ignoring the fact that now you can just banish the spirits from it, once again this is implying that evil doesn't come from our world, it comes from another place, which according to you is part of a 'dark cosmos,' instead of being reflections of the 'real' World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. As Chris said, the First Wound (which, should you be using Inferno rules, is a part of Hell) is a realm drawn to infect the world via acts of native profound evil. As are all the Lower Depths, to steal the Mage term - evil and spiritual desolation are things they cause, but they only <i>exist </i>in the first place when there is evil and spiritual desolation to begin with. They make the problem worse, they don't create it - lung cancer to evil's smoking. Someone still has to smoke to get that kind of lung cancer, even if it's a lot worse than nicotine addiction.<br /> <br /> And frankly, the First Wound wouldn't <i>exist </i>were it not for something very native to the mortal world and Shadow - the death of Father Wolf. This is explicit, it's repeatedly mentioned the Firstborn made the Maeljin whenever the Woundborn come up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T14:42:02-07:00","id":169277,"title":"","content":"I'm mildly concerned that Sacred Hunt returns as a full on ritual when I think it should be baked into the werewolf condition. Not only does it seem like something werewolves should just be able to instinctively tap into, but it once again places spirits in twilight behind an exp wall. If I could make a suggestion, which I'm in no position to do, I'd make the declaration of a hunt and the ability to touch/feed-upon spirits in twilight an intrinsic capacity of the Uratha and then use the rite to anoint it into a Sacred Hunt with proper mechanical and thematic benefits by drawing upon ancient laws of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Also the rite Wellspring seems to imply that werewolves can use Influences. I realize that one of the benefits is that it -gives- you an Influence based on its resonance, but the wording vaguely implies that you can get them from other sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T18:24:09-07:00","id":169384,"title":"","content":"I think a large part of this conversation about how there's probably a baked in condition as well as a ritual. I don't know myself, and I'm content to wait for word from on high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T18:24:54-07:00","id":169385,"title":"","content":"Why should we talk about rituals like they're something not naturally part of the werewolf condition? Rituals aren't some tack-on, they're part of the werewolf experience. If you are completely on your own in the middle of Montana and the nearest Forsaken tutor is in Canada, you can learn rites from spirits. Anyone can learn them. Learning low-level ones is not really any more expensive than learning gifts besides your starting choices.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason rites feel like a tack-on in 1.0 is that it takes forever to collect the 'necessary' rites, and they're all narrow and often dry. The new draft emphasizes the way they enable werewolves to be shamans and real keepers of their territory instead of just cruise-guided muscle and rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T19:04:17-07:00","id":169402,"title":"","content":"Well....Because they aren't.<br /> <br /> Rites may be easy to learn and inherent to the culture, but werewolves aren't just Changed into knowing them. Same with Gifts, really. They are an external, albeit it closely associated, factor in the lives of werewolves. You don't have it when you First Change, you learn it after the fact, and (key point) not everyone does.<br /> <br /> It's like Duct tape-pervasive in the world, yes, but not everyone has a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T19:43:23-07:00","id":169415,"title":"","content":"Not everyone learns it, but a werewolf who has no access to rites is exceedingly unusual and probably eschewing the company of his fellows and proper behavior anyway.<br /> <br /> I could apply these conditions to a bunch of other core game concepts. You don't have a tribal totem when you first change and not everyone picks one. You don't have a pack when you change (most of the time, anyway, now that the chronicle book is switching things up), and not everyone gets one. Same with territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T20:17:05-07:00","id":169431,"title":"","content":"Right, so they aren't a natural part of the werewolf condition. Which is why it's a discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T21:10:04-07:00","id":169460,"title":"","content":"Arguably a lot of things humans do aren't a natural part of the human condition. Are Forsaken the standard for werewolves? They always seemed an exception, striving for something more.<br /> <br /> What happens to a werewolf without a totem or the sacred hunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-15-2014, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T21:29:59-07:00","id":169470,"title":"","content":"Chain Rage is a second line of defense against Kuruth, I kinda wanna know what is the first one, because basing ourselves from what's been shared? that's the only thing that contemplates the prevention of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T21:35:55-07:00","id":169472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169470#post169470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chain Rage is a second line of defense against Kuruth, I kinda wanna know what is the first one, because basing ourselves from what's been shared? that's the only thing that contemplates the prevention of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure the first line of defense is not having borked Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T23:23:27-07:00","id":169528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169277#post169277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mildly concerned that Sacred Hunt returns as a full on ritual when I think it should be baked into the werewolf condition. Not only does it seem like something werewolves should just be able to instinctively tap into, but it once again places spirits in twilight behind an exp wall. If I could make a suggestion, which I'm in no position to do, I'd make the declaration of a hunt and the ability to touch/feed-upon spirits in twilight an intrinsic capacity of the Uratha and then use the rite to anoint it into a Sacred Hunt with proper mechanical and thematic benefits by drawing upon ancient laws of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Also the rite Wellspring seems to imply that werewolves can use Influences. I realize that one of the benefits is that it -gives- you an Influence based on its resonance, but the wording vaguely implies that you can get them from other sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of agree with Sacred Hunt. I also have to ask why (While we haven't gotten the new morality trait yet) it would be a break against Spirit to hunt a spirit. Considering that Spirits do this all the times and even under their hierarchy. It would seem only natural TO kill and devour other spirits from what we've gotten about them across the books.<br /> <br /> Going down the rest of the list.<br /> <br /> Chain Rage seems useful.<br /> <br /> Forge Alliance seems extremely situational. It's powerful though.<br /> <br /> Banish seems like it should be able to force spirits into the material world.<br /> <br /> Totemic Empowerment seems weird to me. It's just the duration of it is short and the drawbacks can be pretty bad while the benefits can be really useful. It seems much better for the pure than the forsaken as it's only as powerful as the totem itself.<br /> <br /> Wellspring is pretty powerful. I don't know if it should grant 5 dots of an influence because you decided to spend five XP though. I'd probably use the person's powerstat or limit it to 1/2 as a human. Considering what happens if you violate the ban it seems like this should last a year and a day.<br /> <br /> For supplication, I'd have to read how the impressions chart works to know how useful it'd be.<br /> <br /> <br /> So here's my full opinions of the totems from most useful to least in my opinion. Sacred hunt feels like it's mandatory which is kind of annoying. If your ritemaster doesn't have it, the team suffers for it until he acquires it. Banish and Wellspring feel like must haves but you don't need them to function. Chain Rage is probably a must have as well but I'd need to see how big of an issue rage is in general to warrant using it. Supplication seems like it'll be needed for wellspring or at least useful. Totemic Empowerment and Forge Alliance are well extremely subjective. If you have a weak Totem what's the point of Empowering it? If you have a pure totem, if you fail a roll it seems like you'll be doing extremely bad things for the rest of the night. I'm not sure the pros outweighs the cons. Forge Alliance requires other willing packs which can be cool for dramatic moments but is paying for a five dot merit for a dramatic moment that might never be used again worth it? This feels like an NPC power rather than something your pcs would do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 06-15-2014, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T23:41:34-07:00","id":169537,"title":"","content":"We got info on the new Harmony. I'm sure someone else will provide the link, but it's back a few weeks.<br /> <br /> It's a balance between your human side, and your wolf/spirit side. Hunting a spirit and taking all of its essence is a break towards spirit because it's a very inhuman thing to do, while also being a very spirit thing to do. Doing it, like you said, is very spirit-like and puts you more towards the spirit side of your balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T00:03:00-07:00","id":169543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=168786#post168786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have only one major complaint.<br /> <br /> That this isn't how the Ceremony system for Geist worked <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I hope it's more structured than that. Geist's system was apparently made purely with the intent of fucking with any Awakened who are trying to get Arcane xp from it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T01:18:43-07:00","id":169599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169148#post169148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's gone, dead. Mechanics for stuff shifting with you are now part of the core shapeshifting rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is important to me, as my now game is having issue of &quot;I lost my clothes with a shapechange&quot; and players are roaming all the territory for they stuff. I thought I could work with that 2-3 sessions, but reality is that this one was pain in the #$% only after first, with all those pack splits and long journeys to get they pair of jeans.<br /> <br /> So how should I resolve this issue with Dedication of items? They suddenly instictivly know after First Change that they can shapechange with they clothes? Or our Itheaur just come up with this idea, and even if it isn't real Rite, he will guide them by it? Also, important question - Primal Urge limit of stuff to change with you is still in place?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169148#post169148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Wounded spirits aren't 'bad' spirits. They're <i>corrupted</i>. Hatred, anger, death, murder, pain, anguish spirits are all perfectly normal spirits. The creatures that infest the pustules of taint that are Wounds have been infected and changed. A Wounded spirit of happiness would be hurled through a Wound by the Banish rite; an unWounded spirit of hatred would not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very interesting, as I now run game about Bale Hounds and Mealjin infestaion in smal toin in Sweden. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169148#post169148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, the purpose of Chain Rage is to offer a trade-off option. On the one hand, it offers a solid second line of protection should Kuruth occur, giving werewolves a solid chance of avoiding entering full Death Rage. However, it does this in return for two things. The first is the certainty of full-on Death Rage at the end of the month. <i>This</i> is supposed to be something that, of course, packs who use Chain Rage will plan around and keep an eye on; you probably want to have some sort of secure place to lock the chap into when it comes to the end of their month under the rite, then let them loose somewhere they can't destroy anything. This, er, may be problematic if they have certain Facets, of course. The second trade-off, though, is the fact you have to have the focus on you. This is a vulnerability - if that focus gets taken or destroyed, boom, death rage. Again, I'd expect packs to do everything they can to protect their rage foci as much as possible, but that doesn't mean the risk isn't there. Canny enemies and pure bad luck can both cause a serious back-fire here.</div> </div> </div> </div>This <b>is</b> great, really! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-15-2014, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T02:31:02-07:00","id":169635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169277#post169277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mildly concerned that Sacred Hunt returns as a full on ritual when I think it should be baked into the werewolf condition.</div> </div> </div> </div> The ability to hit spirits in twilight is partially baked into the werewolf condition through the system for honorary spirit rank and banes. On that note, specifically, remember that banes can harm beings in twilight. I'm also surprised no-one noticed the bit where sacred hunt specifies ephemeral beings, not just spirits <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also the rite Wellspring seems to imply that werewolves can use Influences. I realize that one of the benefits is that it -gives- you an Influence based on its resonance, but the wording vaguely implies that you can get them from other sources. </div> </div> </div> It does indeed imply that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T02:32:21-07:00","id":169636,"title":"","content":"My only gripe is just they seem to need sooooo many symbols (making customs gets complicated). The rule of thumb I'd take, for my own ease of mind there: the symbols there are suggestions, use 1 explicitly per lvl of the rite.<br /> <br /> This brings credence to the fact that a lvl 5 rite is way more complicated than a lvl 1 rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T02:40:37-07:00","id":169644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169528#post169528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wellspring is pretty powerful. I don't know if it should grant 5 dots of an influence because you decided to spend five XP though. I'd probably use the person's powerstat or limit it to 1/2 as a human. Considering what happens if you violate the ban it seems like this should last a year and a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm slightly confused - where do you get the idea of getting 5 dots of Influence for spending five XP? The Influence depends on the strength of the Wellspringed Locus and has no XP cost for anyone who is drawing upon that Influence; it's a temporary benefit, not a permanent one.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T02:49:42-07:00","id":169648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169528#post169528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of agree with Sacred Hunt. I also have to ask why (While we haven't gotten the new morality trait yet) it would be a break against Spirit to hunt a spirit. Considering that Spirits do this all the times and even under their hierarchy. It would seem only natural TO kill and devour other spirits from what we've gotten about them across the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I read it, it's not a breaking point to spirit every time you enact the Sacred Hunt, but only when you take all of their essence and destroy them completely forever, or when you rip the secrets of a gift or rite out of them.<br /> <br /> The fact that destroying a spirit forever is just like what spirits do to each other is part of <i>why </i>it's a breaking point from the fluff perspective - you're acting like a spirit! But from a design perspective, and sort of an IC diplomatic perspective, I think it shows that these are dramatic and somewhat unusual acts of force - it's a bit easier and safer to just discorporate them, bind them, and/or bargain for their secrets. You <i>can </i>just overpower them - that's your power and right. But those are actions with significant consequences and they push your soul in a particular direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T03:08:37-07:00","id":169655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169644#post169644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm slightly confused - where do you get the idea of getting 5 dots of Influence for spending five XP? The Influence depends on the strength of the Wellspringed Locus and has no XP cost for anyone who is drawing upon that Influence; it's a temporary benefit, not a permanent one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe Epimetheus means buying a 5-dot locus as a 5-dot merit. Locus was explicitly not a merit in the original rulebook, and I would think it stays that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T03:40:04-07:00","id":169686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169644#post169644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm slightly confused - where do you get the idea of getting 5 dots of Influence for spending five XP? The Influence depends on the strength of the Wellspringed Locus and has no XP cost for anyone who is drawing upon that Influence; it's a temporary benefit, not a permanent one.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>LIke penta said I confused it with a normal buyable merit (Too many merits to keep track of). However, it's still a relatively easy one to get. Unless the St bans the ability to find Locus' with a strength of 4 or 5 the issue becomes the ability to mass create and create permanent things. Depending on the influence, past 2 dots things get really wonky with influences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T03:46:54-07:00","id":169688,"title":"","content":"Locus isn't Merit? I always thought it is, as with mage Hallow. Especially, as Locus need to be &quot;garden&quot; - which is as much saying &quot;it should be group Merit&quot; as it can only be...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T04:58:09-07:00","id":169698,"title":"","content":"I think there is a narrative difference between Hallows and Loci.<br /> <br /> Loci are very much contested by other werewolf packs and spirits, and they will assault and maybe even kill your pack over it if they show any weakness. A Locus is thus a plot device that they character have little control over. As being a Merit implies some narrative control, it thus should not be a merit.<br /> <br /> Hallows are often part of the Sanctums of Mages, which are well defended using a lot of spells and other game mechanics which Werewolf does not have. In Mage the status quo of a cabal owning a Hallow is often kept (in some kind of cold war state), and otherwise the Consilium could intervene. The players have stable access and thus enough narrative control over the Hallow for it to be a merit.<br /> <br /> In my game I have a distinction between Merits and Backgrounds (now called Story Merits, since a recent thread), where Story Merits are gotten in game, do not cost XP and are at the mercy of the ST. Using this distinction, Locus would be a Story Merit in my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T05:37:52-07:00","id":169712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169635#post169635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The ability to hit spirits in twilight is partially baked into the werewolf condition through the system for honorary spirit rank and banes. On that note, specifically, remember that banes can harm beings in twilight. I'm also surprised no-one noticed the bit where sacred hunt specifies ephemeral beings, not just spirits <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's good to know, as long as it doesn't mean the best way to ambush a werewolf is from Twilight because they'll have to run and find their shaman to do a ritual that will take at least a minute then I'm fine. Blessing of the Spirit Hunt was at least just an instant action. Still a little concerned, but as long as there are options.<br /> <br /> That said I DID notice that it referred to ephemeral beings, which is one of the things I griped about in the old system, and now I'm curious if that means you can call a sacred hunt on angels or ghosts. Or Mages who get a bit cheeky. So good on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169635#post169635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It does indeed imply that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. HMM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T08:41:06-07:00","id":169791,"title":"","content":"From Twilight is generally one of the best ways to ambush people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T09:42:04-07:00","id":169843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169599#post169599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how should I resolve this issue with Dedication of items? They suddenly instictivly know after First Change that they can shapechange with they clothes? Or our Itheaur just come up with this idea, and even if it isn't real Rite, he will guide them by it? Also, important question - Primal Urge limit of stuff to change with you is still in place?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? Until IC comes out, I'd just institute a Don't take The Piss Rule. Their clothes and personal accoutrements shift with them when they shift. If they start trying to define stuff like 'this huge chest full of guns' as part of their personal accoutrements, that is officially Taking The Piss and you should tell them to stop it :P<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169686#post169686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> LIke penta said I confused it with a normal buyable merit (Too many merits to keep track of). However, it's still a relatively easy one to get. Unless the St bans the ability to find Locus' with a strength of 4 or 5 the issue becomes the ability to mass create and create permanent things. Depending on the influence, past 2 dots things get really wonky with influences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, 4 and 5 dot Loci aren't common and they're going to be the subject of serious competition by other packs. If you have a high-dot Locus and you can hold onto it, then enjoy the fruits of your prowess in the form of the Influence dots <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169712#post169712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that's good to know, as long as it doesn't mean the best way to ambush a werewolf is from Twilight because they'll have to run and find their shaman to do a ritual that will take at least a minute then I'm fine. Blessing of the Spirit Hunt was at least just an instant action. Still a little concerned, but as long as there are options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Twilight *is* a great way to launch an ambush. It's supposed to be a problem that has to be overcome. That said, to overcome it you have Rank, Banes, Sacred Hunt, another Rite that fucks Twilight up pretty bad, allied spirits and your Totem in Twilight, and probably some other tools as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said I DID notice that it referred to ephemeral beings, which is one of the things I griped about in the old system, and now I'm curious if that means you can call a sacred hunt on angels or ghosts. Or Mages who get a bit cheeky. So good on that. </div> </div> </div>You can call a hunt on anything - werewolves, spirits, humans, mages, ghosts, angels, Things What Man Was Not Meant To Wot Of, etc.<br /> <br /> I mean, theoretically you could have some crazy werewolf declaring 'I call a Hunt on DEATH ITSELF!' and shaking their fist in defiance at the skies. Good luck finding the prey though :P<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hm. HMM. </div> </div> </div>INDEED.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T09:49:27-07:00","id":169844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, theoretically you could have some crazy werewolf declaring 'I call a Hunt on DEATH ITSELF!' and shaking their fist in defiance at the skies. Good luck finding the prey though.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's actually a really cool set up for a chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T11:22:37-07:00","id":169933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169843#post169843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? Until IC comes out, I'd just institute a Don't take The Piss Rule. Their clothes and personal accoutrements shift with them when they shift. If they start trying to define stuff like 'this huge chest full of guns' as part of their personal accoutrements, that is officially Taking The Piss and you should tell them to stop it :P</div> </div> </div> </div>My question is more HOW the Pack would get idea of this - suddenly, they want to change with clothes and they can? Or just, randomly, one character can left with they pants on under change to Urshul, after k10 changes? Or is it Ithaeur get idea after looking over many shapeshifting lore in myths and say &quot;You can change with clothes on you&quot;?<br /> <br /> You wrote it's more instinctual to characters now - and that's why it isn't Rite - so I would want at least a guide on this, if you can. I will assume Primal Urge limit, because I see it will be left. Only I should strife to &quot;you get it with your new wolf sences&quot; or &quot;your Ithaeurn makes a pseudo-Rite on you, and you 'remember' how to do it&quot;. What would you advise with <b>IC</b> changes in mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T11:26:14-07:00","id":169936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169933#post169933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My question is more HOW the Pack would get idea of this - suddenly, they want to change with clothes and they can? Or just, randomly, one character can left with they pants on under change to Urshul, after k10 changes? Or is it Ithaeur get idea after looking over many shapeshifting lore in myths and say &amp;quot;You can change with clothes on you&amp;quot;? You wrote it's more instinctual to characters now - and that's why it isn't Rite - so I would want at least a guide on this, if you can. I will assume Primal Urge limit, because I see it will be left. Only I should strife to &amp;quot;you get it with your new wolf sences&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;your Ithaeurn makes a pseudo-Rite on you, and you 'remember' how to do it&amp;quot;. What would you advise with <b>IC</b> changes in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think it's something the character consciously does. You don't have to learn it, or remember it, or have the idea to do it. You just shapeshift and your clothes shapeshift with you. Presumably even on your First Change , it's just part of how Shapeshifting works now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T12:33:18-07:00","id":170000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169843#post169843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">allied spirits</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really pleased this is an actual thing now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T12:56:41-07:00","id":170044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169936#post169936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't think it's something the character consciously does. You don't have to learn it, or remember it, or have the idea to do it. You just shapeshift and your clothes shapeshift with you. Presumably even on your First Change , it's just part of how Shapeshifting works now.</div> </div> </div> </div>So were would go all &quot;you woke up in torn clothes&quot; cliche of werewolf stories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T13:10:12-07:00","id":170049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/168761-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-rites?p=169843#post169843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, theoretically you could have some crazy werewolf declaring 'I call a Hunt on DEATH ITSELF!' and shaking their fist in defiance at the skies. Good luck finding the prey though :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems simple enough. Kill a rabbit and wait for Death to show up. Just don't be surprised when it says &quot;<span style=\"font-size:10px\">THAT WAS A POINTLESS EXERCISE IN GETTING MY ATTENTION.&quot; </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T13:36:53-07:00","id":170075,"title":"","content":"YOU SUMMONED ME?<br /> <img src=\"http://zoegraves.files.wordpress.com/2012/12/tumblr_m7k4m81q3b1qhtj9io1_400.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user"